<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠγ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ὁ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span>:
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φεύγω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who flees</i> from his country, either
			voluntarily, <i>runaway, fugitive,</i> or by legal sentence,
				<i>exile,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.150
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.138
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεκηρύχθην φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					430
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξελήλαμαι φ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1292
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. πάσης τῆς χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.1.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς πατρίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					2.145b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. τῆς τῶν ἐξελασάντων πονηρίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.92
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἐξ Ἤλιδος, ἐκ Λαρίσης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.2.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.4.34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυγάδ᾽ ἀπ᾽ οὐρανοῦ θεόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					214
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἐξ Ἀθηνῶν ὑπὸ Ἀθηναίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					1.5.19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. παρ᾽ ὑμῶν</span>
			<i>a deserter</i> from . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.3.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθεν . . εἰμὶ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.6.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς δὲ φ. ἐντεῦθεν ἐποίησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					13.64
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.1.40
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάγειν φυγάδας</span> to
			restore <i>them,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.31
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. καθεῖναι, καταδέχεσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.2.10
			</span></i>: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἐλπίδες βόσκουσι φυγάδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					396
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ φ. πύλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.46
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδένα εἶναι . . ὑπερορίαν
				φυγάδα,</span> is dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				855c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of an army,
				<i>put to flight,</i><i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				108
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
